@*
    "Keep me signed in", and the period it promises, in one place.

    Every screen that starts a sign-in shows this -- the hand-off at /login and the
    two invite landings -- because an option that appears on one route into the app
    and not the others is a worse promise than no option at all.

    The number here is copy. What actually ends the session is
    RememberedSessionLifetime on the server, and the two have to say the same thing.
*@

<div style="width: 100%; text-align: start">
    <MudCheckBox T="bool"
                 Value="Value"
                 ValueChanged="ValueChanged"
                 Color="Color.Primary"
                 Dense="true"
                 Disabled="Disabled"
                 Label="Keep me signed in" />
    <p class="gs-muted" style="margin: 0 0 0 32px; font-size: .75rem">
        Stays signed in on this browser for @Days days. Uncheck to sign out automatically when you close the browser.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Kept in step with <c>AuthenticationExtensions.RememberedSessionLifetime</c>.</summary>
    public const int Days = 30;

    [Parameter] public bool Value { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Set once the hand-off is under way, so the answer cannot change after it was sent.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }
}
